# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# This repo is deliberately SELF-CONTAINED: it carries only the credentials it
# actually needs, rather than reusing a shared multi-provider dotenv. That is a
# security decision, not a style one -- this repository is public, and a shared
# dotenv would stage every unrelated provider key behind a single push.

# --- Alpaca, account C: the submission account -------------------------------
# From app.alpaca.markets -> Home -> API Keys. PAPER keys start with "PK".
# Never put live keys here: nothing in this repo passes --live, and the paper
# host cannot touch real money regardless.
#
# Each book names its own key variables in its rulebook's `account` block, and
# `assert_account` in agent/agent_loop.py refuses to start when the credentials
# these resolve to reach a different account than the book names. That guard is
# the reason two books can run side by side without silently sharing one account.
ALPACA_API_KEY_C=PK...
ALPACA_SECRET_KEY_C=

# --- Alpaca, account B: the second book --------------------------------------
ALPACA_API_KEY_B=PK...
ALPACA_SECRET_KEY_B=

# --- Alpaca, default ---------------------------------------------------------
# Used by any invocation that does not pass --profile. Both shipped books name
# their own variables above, so these are only needed for ad-hoc CLI work.
ALPACA_API_KEY=PK...
ALPACA_SECRET_KEY=

# --- LLM for the news-classification step ------------------------------------
# Required for the live agent, not for backtests. Without it the decision step
# resolves to PASS -- the agent degrades to "trade nothing", never to "trade
# without the check".
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Optional ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Set to 1 to force every order through --dry-run regardless of other settings.
# The agent also honours the --shadow flag; this is the belt-and-braces version.
SHADOW=0
